---
// Server-rendered: lab.malipetek.dev/agents has to be able to 301 here.
export const prerender = false;

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/kb.css';

const PORTAL_TOOLS = [
  { name: "portal_projects / portal_requests / portal_request", auth: "client key", text: "The account's projects and requests, with status and cost." },
  { name: "portal_file_request", auth: "client key", text: "File a request for Ali. Nothing starts until he reads it." },
  { name: "portal_reply", auth: "client key", text: "Add a message to a request's conversation." },
  { name: "portal_set_budget", auth: "client key", text: "Raise, lower or remove a request's budget." },
  { name: "portal_withdraw", auth: "client key", text: "Take back a request Ali has not approved yet." },
];
---

<Base
  title="Connect your assistant — M. Ali Petek"
  description="One MCP endpoint for the client portal: file and follow website requests from ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor or any MCP client."
  current="/agents"
>
  <main class="wrap kb">
    <header class="kb-head">
      <p class="kb-kicker">Model Context Protocol</p>
      <h1>Connect your assistant.</h1>
      <p class="kb-lede">
        <a href="/mcp"><code>https://malipetek.dev/mcp</code></a> is the client portal
        over MCP: streamable HTTP, protocol <code>2025-06-18</code>. An assistant with
        your key can file requests, reply, set a budget and follow what happens, all on
        your own account. Every request still goes to Ali before any work starts.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="kb-block">
      <h2>Connect, per client</h2>
      <div class="kb-prose">
        <p>
          One URL: <code>https://malipetek.dev/mcp</code>. Discovery is also published at
          <a href="/.well-known/mcp-server.json"><code>/.well-known/mcp-server.json</code></a>.
        </p>

        <h3>ChatGPT</h3>
        <p>
          Turn on <strong>Settings → Connectors → Advanced → Developer mode</strong>, then
          add a connector:
        </p>
        <pre><code>Name:  malipetek.dev
URL:   https://malipetek.dev/mcp
Auth:  Bearer cat_…   # the key from your portal</code></pre>

        <h3>Claude, Cursor, anything else</h3>
        <p>
          Same URL. In Claude: <strong>Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector</strong>.
          In Cursor, <code>mcp.json</code>:
        </p>
        <pre><code>&#123; "mcpServers": &#123; "malipetek": &#123; "url": "https://malipetek.dev/mcp" &#125; &#125; &#125;</code></pre>

        <h3>No client at all</h3>
        <pre><code>curl -s https://malipetek.dev/mcp -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -H "authorization: Bearer cat_…" \
  -d '&#123;"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list"&#125;'</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="kb-block">
      <h2>Your key</h2>
      <div class="kb-prose">
        <p>
          <a href="/portal">Sign in to the portal</a>, open <em>Connect an assistant</em>, and
          make a key named after the tool that will hold it (<code>chatgpt</code>,
          <code>cursor</code>…). It is shown once and stored hashed. Revoking it is one click.
        </p>
        <p>
          A client's key sees exactly that client's account: the same routes the portal's
          own pages use. It cannot see another client, and it cannot publish or deploy
          anything. ChatGPT can also run the OAuth flow on its own, which ends at the same
          place.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="kb-block">
      <h2>What an assistant can do</h2>
      <ul class="kb-tool-list">
        {PORTAL_TOOLS.map((tool) => (
          <li>
            <code>{tool.name}</code>
            <span class="kb-tool-auth">{tool.auth}</span>
            <span class="kb-tool-text">{tool.text}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="kb-entry-foot">
        The assistant can also work on a change itself, on the client's own subscription:
        read the project's source, send a change on the request's branch, and build it to
        a preview. Those tools are <code>project_context</code>, <code>workspace_files</code>,
        <code>workspace_read</code>, <code>submit_change</code> and <code>preview_build</code>.
        Ali still checks the result before it ships.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="kb-block">
      <h2>The knowledgebase is a separate site</h2>
      <div class="kb-prose">
        <p>
          Ali's agentic coding knowledgebase, the plugins and the writing live at
          <a href="https://lab.malipetek.dev">lab.malipetek.dev</a>. That site has its own
          MCP endpoint at <code>https://lab.malipetek.dev/mcp</code>, with knowledgebase
          tools only. Nothing there is needed to use the portal.
        </p>
        <p>
          Setup for that endpoint is at
          <a href="https://lab.malipetek.dev/kb/agents">lab.malipetek.dev/kb/agents</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
